<%
# ============================================================================
# MISSION 5: INSIDER TRADING - SCENARIO FILE
# ============================================================================
# Break Escape - Season 1: The Architect's Shadow
#
# This file defines the game world structure: rooms, NPCs, objects, items
# For mission metadata (display name, CyBOK mappings, etc.), see mission.json
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (pass 2: single connections only, see PASS2_IMPROVEMENTS.md):
#
#   torres_office      data_center
#        |                  |
#   research_lab - open_office_area    server_room
#                       |                  |
#   break_room - main_corridor ------- server_hallway (RFID)
#                       |
#                reception_lobby ----- patricia_office
#
#   The old layout hung three 10-wide rooms off the 10-wide corridor's north
#   wall. positionNorthMultiple (rooms.js:1253) cannot give all three the
#   1 GU of overlap it needs, so at least one door opened onto nothing.
#   Every connection is now a single E/W pair or an equal-width N/S pair,
#   which always line up (see the m04 door-alignment rule).
#
# THE CASE (pass 2): evidence is a set of found_* booleans, not a counter.
#   The engine assigns setVariable values literally, so the old
#   "evidence_level + 1" strings never counted anything.
#   Motive:  found_medical_bills | found_torres_journal | found_vetting_file
#   Exfil:   flag3_submitted | found_manifest | found_upload_schedule
#   Patricia will act on a name only when the player has one of each.
#
# THE LOCKS (pass 3, PUZZLE_CHAINS_PLAN.md):
#   Start kit: phone, picks (m01), RFID cloner (m03), fingerprint kit (m04).
#   server_hallway  rfid      clone Owen's lanyard (by design), or Dr
#                             Halloran's spare, or HaX's relay
#   server_room     password  Owen refuses by default; Patricia's incident
#                             log (evidence) or her authority opens him up
#   torres_office   rfid      Owen's spare, on Patricia's authority
#   data_center     biometric the key vault, enrolled to Torres alone; his
#                             print is on the mug in his office. Owen names
#                             the reader when he hands over the password
#   briefcase, Patricia's cabinet: picks (by design)
#   Naming: Patricia in person, Patricia by phone (patricia_phone), or HaX.
#
# HYBRID ARCHITECTURE:
#   - VM: Bludit CMS research portal (leaked credentials, authenticated
#     image-upload RCE, then user and root on the box)
#   - 4 VM flags; concludeRequires gates the ending on all four
# ============================================================================

# Narrative Content Variables
server_room_password = "quantum2024"
password_hint_sticky = "Server room temp password (expires Friday): #{server_room_password}\n\n- O"
torres_journal_excerpt = "Met the Recruiter again. Debt relief plus a standing retainer if I finish the upload tonight. Elena's first trial dose is Monday.\n\nI know what this costs. Thirty to forty-five people, by their own projections. Ambulances that don't arrive in time.\n\nI've talked myself round with their philosophy. The system is rotten. Collateral damage for the greater good.\n\nI read that back and I don't recognise the man who wrote it. What have I become?"
