  <%# PASS 2: every task is "active" (the m02 pattern). unlockAim activates only
      an aim's FIRST task (objectives-manager.js:651-660) and handleItemPickup
      ignores any task that isn't active (:324), so with "locked" tasks the
      collect/enter tasks in later aims could never tick. Notes-type evidence
      is matched with targetItemIds: targetItems matches the item TYPE, and
      every one of these items is type "notes". %>
  <%# PASS 2 review (lesson 27): a locked aim auto-reveals when any of its
      tasks completes (objectives-manager.js:414-419). Tasks now sit in the aim
      where the player meets them: the sticky note, the leaflet and the vetting
      file are first-ring finds, so they live in aim 2. "Find Out Why" and
      "Prove the Exfiltration" both open from aim 2 and run in parallel,
      because nothing in the rooms orders them. The aims are a to-do list, not
      a gate: doors, items and concludeRequires are what gate progress. %>
